WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.687
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:05.987 --> 00:00:09.466
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:16.807
Unit twenty-one: Transport and Road Safety News. Today you will describe numbers and amounts with quantifiers.

4
00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:19.771
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:24.338
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:26.022
Traffic.

7
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:29.713
Traffic means the vehicles moving along a road.

8
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:32.665
Heavy traffic slowed the morning commute.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.100
Your turn. Say: Traffic.

10
00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:39.772
Traffic.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.645
Road safety.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.078
Road safety means keeping people safe when they use roads.

13
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.054
Road safety lessons begin at school.

14
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.964
Your turn. Say: Road safety.

15
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.975
Road safety.

16
00:00:57.717 --> 00:00:58.544
Helmet.

17
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.153
Helmet means a hard hat that protects the head.

18
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.808
A helmet saved the rider's life.

19
00:01:05.417 --> 00:01:08.220
Your turn. Say: Helmet.

20
00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:11.998
Helmet.

21
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.670
Accident.

22
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:18.181
Accident means an unexpected event that causes harm or damage.

23
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:20.527
The accident closed the bridge.

24
00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:24.001
Your turn. Say: Accident.

25
00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:27.670
Accident.

26
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:29.685
Infrastructure.

27
00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:35.156
Infrastructure means roads, bridges and other basic public structures.

28
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.063
New infrastructure improved the city.

29
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:41.883
Your turn. Say: Infrastructure.

30
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:46.257
Infrastructure.

31
00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:47.960
Commuter.

32
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.587
Commuter means a person who travels regularly to work or school.

33
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:55.357
Every commuter waited at the station.

34
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.138
Your turn. Say: Commuter.

35
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:01.839
Commuter.

36
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:03.701
Statistics.

37
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:07.947
Statistics means numbers that describe facts about something.

38
00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.909
Statistics show that accidents are falling.

39
00:02:11.517 --> 00:02:14.250
Your turn. Say: Statistics.

40
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.461
Statistics.

41
00:02:19.217 --> 00:02:20.218
Campaign.

42
00:02:21.217 --> 00:02:24.064
Campaign means an organised effort to achieve a goal.

43
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.137
The helmet campaign reached every province.

44
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.344
Your turn. Say: Campaign.

45
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.073
Campaign.

46
00:02:34.867 --> 00:02:38.378
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:46.919
Visal, the report says 'A number of accidents involve motorbikes, and the majority of riders were not wearing helmets.' What do those phrases mean?

48
00:02:48.017 --> 00:02:56.570
They are quantifiers. 'A number of' means several and 'the majority of' means more than half. They are common in statistics.

49
00:02:57.683 --> 00:02:58.951
Are there others?

50
00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:09.750
Yes: a few, most, many, a large proportion of, hardly any. With plural nouns the verb is plural: most commuters use the bus.

51
00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.687
And with uncountable nouns?

52
00:03:13.783 --> 00:03:24.029
Use much, a great deal of or little: 'Much of the infrastructure is old.' A road safety campaign can then target the problem.

53
00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.015
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.802
Grammar focus: Quantifiers in statistics.

55
00:03:31.102 --> 00:03:32.242
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.809
The majority of riders were not wearing helmets.

57
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:39.355
A number of accidents involve motorbikes.

58
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.389
Much of the infrastructure is old.

59
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:50.885
Use many / a number of / the majority of with plural nouns, and much / a great deal of with uncountable nouns. The verb agrees with the noun.

60
00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.929
Be careful! Don't say: Much of the roads are old.

61
00:03:56.867 --> 00:03:59.412
Say: Many of the roads are old.

62
00:03:59.712 --> 00:04:01.363
Many goes with plural nouns.

63
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.865
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:06.668
On the Road.

65
00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:11.336
Statistics show that road accidents remain a serious problem in many cities.

66
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:16.690
The majority of victims are motorbike riders, and many were not wearing a helmet.

67
00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.950
Much of the infrastructure is old, so heavy traffic makes every commute more dangerous.

68
00:04:23.967 --> 00:04:27.696
A number of campaigns now teach commuters about road safety.

69
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.768
Better habits and better roads together can save lives.

70
00:04:32.867 --> 00:04:36.764
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:37.617 --> 00:04:40.394
The majority of riders blank not wearing helmets.

72
00:04:40.694 --> 00:04:43.628
A, were. B, was. C, is.

73
00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:48.737
The answer is A: were.

74
00:04:49.883 --> 00:04:52.394
Roads and bridges are part of a country's blank.

75
00:04:52.694 --> 00:04:56.591
A, infrastructure. B, campaign. C, commuter.

76
00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.818
The answer is A: infrastructure.

77
00:05:03.983 --> 00:05:06.308
A hard hat that protects the head is a blank.

78
00:05:06.608 --> 00:05:10.424
A, helmet. B, statistic. C, traffic.

79
00:05:13.967 --> 00:05:15.815
The answer is A: helmet.

80
00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.694
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:18.994 --> 00:05:24.703
A, Much of the roads are old.. B, Many of the roads are old.. C, Many of the road is old..

82
00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:31.067
The answer is B: Many of the roads are old..

83
00:05:32.217 --> 00:05:35.923
According to the reading, a number of blank teach road safety.

84
00:05:36.223 --> 00:05:40.039
A, campaigns. B, helmets. C, victims.

85
00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.820
The answer is A: campaigns.

86
00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:50.440
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:53.945
What transport issue most affects your city?

88
00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.204
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:04.504 --> 00:06:25.888
The transport issue that most affects my city is heavy traffic. Many commuters spend a long time on the road, and a number of accidents happen at busy junctions. Better public transport and safer infrastructure could help. If more people used buses, there would be fewer vehicles and fewer accidents.

90
00:06:26.188 --> 00:06:27.758
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.218
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and quantifiers in statistics.

92
00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:37.680
Today's value is road safety. Look left and right, and wear a helmet.

93
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.922
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:41.222 --> 00:06:43.921
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

